    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just hard to see it as a \"victory\" when it feels so pointless. everything is just... repetitive. i feel like a machine that’s been decommissioned but is still being forced to run on an empty battery. if a patient came to me with no life left to save, no more utility, no more function... i'd understand why they couldn't go on. i just wonder if there's any actual dignity in just dragging it out for the sake of it.",
